WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:03.969
A long, long time ago.

00:03.970 --> 00:06.770
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:07.640 --> 00:12.380
Nadja, guided by
destiny, arrived in France.

00:16.640 --> 00:17.440
- NAAJA
- Nadja,

00:18.000 --> 00:19.270
With your eyes

00:19.271 --> 00:20.539
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:20.540 --> 00:21.750
- Nadja,
- NAAJA

00:21.753 --> 00:22.880
What do you see?

00:22.881 --> 00:24.010
Nani ga mieru

00:24.210 --> 00:25.650
Shining in the far distance,

00:25.651 --> 00:27.090
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.220 --> 00:28.325
The door to the future,

00:28.326 --> 00:29.430
Mirai no tobira

00:30.320 --> 00:31.940
That's what I'm searching for

00:31.941 --> 00:33.560
Sagashite iru

00:34.180 --> 00:37.650
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:41.660 --> 00:43.540
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:43.541 --> 00:45.420
Minna egao de aetara

00:45.540 --> 00:48.790
- I'm sure there would be no more fighting
- Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:48.920 --> 00:50.525
It could be so much more fun

00:50.526 --> 00:52.130
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.210 --> 00:53.920
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:53.921 --> 00:55.630
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.050 --> 00:57.700
I can't see the end of the journey

00:57.701 --> 00:59.350
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.390 --> 01:02.720
- God is the only one who could
possibly know - Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:02.850 --> 01:06.440
- To the people who, someday, I will meet
again - Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:06.443 --> 01:07.500
I will go waving

01:07.501 --> 01:08.560
Te wo furinagara

01:08.860 --> 01:12.175
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:12.176 --> 01:15.489
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.490 --> 01:16.845
But I won't look back

01:16.846 --> 01:18.200
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.450 --> 01:20.930
Until the day my dream comes true

01:20.931 --> 01:23.410
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:23.660 --> 01:25.370
Nadja, Your smile

01:25.371 --> 01:27.079
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.080 --> 01:28.750
Nadja, gives me courage

01:28.751 --> 01:30.420
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:30.630 --> 01:32.090
Under the blue sky,

01:32.091 --> 01:33.549
Aoi sora no shita de

01:33.550 --> 01:34.965
I will find the place

01:34.966 --> 01:36.380
Ashita no yukue

01:36.970 --> 01:38.785
where my future lies

01:38.786 --> 01:40.600
Mitsukeru kara

01:50.020 --> 01:52.400
It's Black Rose! Black Rose has appeared!

01:57.310 --> 01:58.900
Black Rose has–

02:02.310 --> 02:03.310
My–

02:03.650 --> 02:06.540
My precious collection!

02:17.760 --> 02:18.760
Hmm?

02:23.740 --> 02:26.490
This painting... was
the one stolen from us.

02:30.680 --> 02:33.900
"I have escorted back
the Damsel in Distress."

02:34.610 --> 02:35.610
Black Rose?!

02:42.760 --> 02:46.760
The Masquerade Ball Trap

02:50.130 --> 02:54.629
It seems that the phantom thief Black Rose has
stolen a painting from that upstart, Lubich.

02:54.630 --> 02:58.589
That painting was stolen from the
Louvre a long time ago, wasn't it?

02:58.590 --> 03:03.359
Lubich bought the painting with
dirty money, then kept it privately.

03:03.360 --> 03:06.619
So that's why Black Rose
returned it to the musuem.

03:06.620 --> 03:08.349
That guy is no common thief!

03:08.350 --> 03:12.650
Black Rose is a hero who returned
France's national treasure from criminals!

03:13.070 --> 03:14.860
Black Rose is a hero!

03:19.740 --> 03:22.619
<i>Miss Appleton, are you well?</i>

03:22.620 --> 03:25.259
<i>I'm living in Paris right now.</i>

03:25.260 --> 03:28.379
<i>How's everyone in Applefield doing?</i>

03:28.380 --> 03:30.430
Black Rose has done it again!

03:31.600 --> 03:34.439
That guy really is on the
side of the commoners!

03:34.440 --> 03:36.510
"Black Rose" is just like Nezumi Kozo.

03:36.940 --> 03:38.680
Nezumi Kozo?

03:39.300 --> 03:43.890
A long time ago in my homeland
of Japan, he was a famous thief.

03:44.370 --> 03:48.769
It's said he stole money from the
wicked and scattered it amongst the poor.

03:48.770 --> 03:49.829
A chivalrous thief!

03:49.830 --> 03:50.350
Really?

03:50.351 --> 03:52.070
Chivalrous thieves, in Japan?

03:51.190 --> 03:52.730
<i>Black Rose?</i>

03:52.070 --> 03:53.600
But why is he called Nezumi?

03:52.730 --> 03:54.530
<i>That man came to France?</i>

03:55.150 --> 03:58.900
You're so thin, skinny girl.

03:59.240 --> 04:00.419
<i>That guy!</i>

04:00.420 --> 04:04.200
<i>Even if he punishes bad
people, a thief is still a thief!</i>

04:14.040 --> 04:16.670
I can't believe that Black
Rose has turned up in Paris.

04:17.130 --> 04:20.409
I can just see that upstart
Lubich raging over this.

04:20.410 --> 04:22.940
Can't you, Madame Monterlant?

04:24.840 --> 04:30.860
To come all the way from England to bring
back a treasure of France, he's very odd.

04:31.440 --> 04:32.650
But interesting.

04:33.590 --> 04:34.719
Everyone!

04:34.720 --> 04:37.610
I have an idea for a splendid party.

04:38.110 --> 04:39.149
Fernando.

04:39.150 --> 04:40.610
Yes, Aunt?

04:40.990 --> 04:43.570
Can you please have the
chauffeur bring the car around?

04:43.940 --> 04:44.940
Yes!

04:57.030 --> 04:59.150
Magnificent!

05:04.000 --> 05:05.140
Anna Petrova?

05:06.600 --> 05:11.399
Oh my, if it isn't Master Leonardo
of the Cardinale Company.

05:11.400 --> 05:12.730
What brings you to Paris?

05:13.190 --> 05:15.860
I had some textile deals to close up here.

05:16.330 --> 05:18.569
This man here is Thierry Rothschild.

05:18.570 --> 05:21.450
He has an exclusive dress
shop on Faubourg Saint-Honore.

05:22.420 --> 05:25.640
I brought him because he
wanted to see your work.

05:26.160 --> 05:27.830
I am honored to make your acquaintance.

05:29.020 --> 05:31.120
And the young lady over there?

05:31.480 --> 05:33.850
My girlfriend, Lady Therese.

05:34.660 --> 05:38.090
Actually, I wanted to ask
you to make a hat for her.

05:38.430 --> 05:41.299
Oh my, that young lady as well?

05:41.300 --> 05:45.550
I wonder, how many girlfriends
does Mr. Leonardo have?

05:45.850 --> 05:47.220
Leonardo!

05:47.860 --> 05:50.440
Everything beautiful in the world is mine.

05:51.120 --> 05:51.560
My...

05:52.140 --> 05:53.320
Granny!

05:53.980 --> 05:55.979
My hem has come off its seams.

05:55.980 --> 05:57.019
Okay.

05:57.020 --> 05:58.040
A new member?

05:58.440 --> 06:00.430
Yes, her name is Nadja.

06:01.830 --> 06:03.360
Oh, how splendid.

06:04.520 --> 06:05.820
Here, that should do it.

06:06.440 --> 06:07.700
Thanks Granny!

06:08.150 --> 06:10.709
Ah, truly splendid.

06:10.710 --> 06:12.200
Little Rosebud.

06:12.580 --> 06:13.580
Eh?

06:13.950 --> 06:16.540
I'm talking about you, my little Rosebud.

06:17.130 --> 06:19.960
But, my name is Nadja.

06:24.610 --> 06:26.390
Well then, thanks for waiting!

06:28.270 --> 06:31.760
The miraculous dancing princess
who has landed in Paris: Nadja!

06:39.180 --> 06:41.800
Well done, my little Rosebud.

06:41.920 --> 06:42.920
Hey!

06:45.190 --> 06:47.659
Everything beautiful
in the world is all mine.

06:47.660 --> 06:49.629
But, that girl is just a bud.

06:49.630 --> 06:50.910
She's no match for you,

06:51.470 --> 06:52.730
my White Lily.

06:53.400 --> 06:54.400
My...

07:00.630 --> 07:02.939
Hey, where did Nadja go?

07:02.940 --> 07:05.089
Ah, she's gone looking for Rita.

07:05.090 --> 07:07.589
Ah, then I'll go look for her, too.

07:07.590 --> 07:08.510
It's okay.

07:08.511 --> 07:10.049
They'll come back soon.

07:10.050 --> 07:12.569
Rita, where are you?

07:12.570 --> 07:13.570
It's lunchtime!

07:17.780 --> 07:19.310
Ah, there she is.

07:31.750 --> 07:32.750
Rita!

07:46.070 --> 07:47.179
Miss!

07:47.180 --> 07:48.430
Are you all right?

07:52.250 --> 07:54.520
Ah! It's all busted!

07:56.940 --> 07:58.149
It's all your fault!

07:58.150 --> 07:59.940
What do you plan to do about this?

08:02.460 --> 08:03.659
What is it?

08:03.660 --> 08:05.070
Apologize properly!

08:07.640 --> 08:08.700
Wait!

08:11.000 --> 08:12.109
Sorry!

08:12.110 --> 08:14.160
This child can't speak.

08:16.490 --> 08:18.569
So, I'll apologize in her place.

08:18.570 --> 08:19.580
We're very sorry.

08:22.590 --> 08:24.809
A mere apology won't cut it.

08:24.810 --> 08:26.230
Just look at that!

08:31.040 --> 08:32.089
I don't have...

08:32.090 --> 08:34.389
any money to pay you with.

08:34.390 --> 08:37.209
But, I'll work to pay for it!

08:37.210 --> 08:39.389
I'll do anything I can!

08:39.390 --> 08:40.409
Hmph!

08:40.410 --> 08:43.259
Do you know how expensive an automobile is?

08:43.260 --> 08:46.820
Even if you worked for the rest of
your lives, you'll never be able to pay!

08:49.010 --> 08:50.249
In this age,

08:50.250 --> 08:52.919
automobiles were extremely rare objects.

08:52.920 --> 08:57.490
Only certain people like aristocrats
and the wealthy were able to ride them.

08:58.760 --> 09:01.330
What admirable sentiments.

09:01.740 --> 09:03.260
Pretty little dancing girl.

09:06.560 --> 09:07.670
Aunt...

09:08.040 --> 09:09.430
What is your name?

09:10.130 --> 09:11.659
It's Nadja.

09:11.660 --> 09:14.589
I dance for the Dandelion Troupe.

09:14.590 --> 09:17.359
My, a travelling performer?

09:17.360 --> 09:19.099
With a body like yours,

09:19.100 --> 09:21.750
I wonder what sort of
indecent dance you do.

09:22.750 --> 09:24.119
What do you mean by "indecent"?!

09:24.120 --> 09:26.520
Everyone enjoys my dance!

09:28.380 --> 09:30.339
My, pardon me.

09:30.340 --> 09:34.910
Then won't you perform this dance
you're so proud of at my house tonight?

09:35.350 --> 09:36.350
Eh?

09:36.940 --> 09:39.040
You said you'd do anything, didn't you?

09:40.310 --> 09:41.399
What's wrong?

09:41.400 --> 09:42.580
Are you all talk then?

09:42.990 --> 09:44.750
I'm not all talk, but...

09:49.640 --> 09:51.109
I understand.

09:51.110 --> 09:52.630
I'll dance.

09:52.910 --> 09:54.030
Ehh?!

09:55.120 --> 09:56.330
Eh-hehe...

09:57.300 --> 09:59.560
So, you said you'll go?

09:59.940 --> 10:01.079
I don't believe it.

10:01.080 --> 10:03.520
She's a lady of wealth you say?

10:03.860 --> 10:05.359
Yes. Simone...

10:05.360 --> 10:07.939
Simone Monterlant was her name.

10:07.940 --> 10:08.980
Madame Monterlant?

10:09.800 --> 10:12.859
Isn't she that famous widow,
who's known even outside of Paris?

10:12.860 --> 10:14.990
You don't hear anything
good about her though.

10:17.350 --> 10:19.200
C'mon Nadja, don't go.

10:22.080 --> 10:23.289
It'll be fine.

10:23.290 --> 10:25.580
I'll come back right after
I show them my dance.

10:26.700 --> 10:28.349
<i>Indecent dance, she says.</i>

10:28.350 --> 10:30.710
<i>I just have to prove to her otherwise!</i>

10:31.240 --> 10:33.710
Oh well. Everything in life is a lesson.

10:58.440 --> 11:01.740
<i>I can come back as soon
as I show them my dance.</i>

11:07.350 --> 11:10.130
Everyone, welcome to my party.

11:13.090 --> 11:16.940
Tonight, as always, I intend to
give you the greatest evening!

11:30.050 --> 11:31.050
Black Rose?

11:32.820 --> 11:34.440
Bonsoir, Mademoiselle.

11:44.140 --> 11:46.729
<i>Why are there so many Black Roses?</i>

11:46.730 --> 11:48.900
<i>Who are these people?</i>

12:14.800 --> 12:19.240
For the man who crossed an
ocean to recover France's treasure –

12:19.480 --> 12:23.540
tonight's masquerade party is in
honor of the phantom thief, Black Rose.

12:24.120 --> 12:25.430
<i>Masquerade party?</i>

12:25.820 --> 12:27.220
When the police found out,

12:27.280 --> 12:30.990
there was a huge fuss
about having this party.

12:31.300 --> 12:34.660
"What happens if the real one appears
among the masqueraders?" they asked.

12:34.940 --> 12:39.020
But, I would gladly extend
my invitation to the real one.

12:39.070 --> 12:41.260
Or so I told them.

12:42.520 --> 12:44.120
That Madame Monterlant.

12:44.270 --> 12:45.730
She says that, but,

12:45.790 --> 12:48.220
if the real one appeared,
she's sure to have a fit.

12:49.240 --> 12:51.810
She's just a show-off.

12:52.210 --> 12:53.900
Well then, to Black Rose!

12:54.140 --> 12:55.430
To Black Rose!

12:56.270 --> 12:57.300
You're late,

12:57.780 --> 12:58.650
dancing girl.

12:58.750 --> 12:59.240
Eh?

12:59.320 --> 13:00.320
Aunt!

13:00.430 --> 13:01.430
Come.

13:03.610 --> 13:04.720
Ah!

13:05.190 --> 13:07.700
Aunt, the dancing girl is here.

13:08.270 --> 13:09.410
Everyone,

13:09.470 --> 13:12.580
because Black Rose is
a champion of the people,

13:12.720 --> 13:16.600
we will have this girl dance as
a representative of the people.

13:16.640 --> 13:17.480
Eh?

13:17.640 --> 13:18.650
Excuse me...

13:20.810 --> 13:22.060
Now, Nadja.

13:22.160 --> 13:25.750
Can you please perform for
everyone this dance you're so proud of?

13:25.960 --> 13:26.450
Eh?

13:26.530 --> 13:28.820
Nadja, go on.

13:33.050 --> 13:34.190
Hey, look.

13:34.410 --> 13:34.850
Yeah.

13:35.240 --> 13:36.420
How interesting.

13:36.600 --> 13:39.340
That girl is mixing
where she doesn't belong.

13:39.770 --> 13:41.260
I know her.

13:41.450 --> 13:44.740
She was dancing in the park today,
with a troupe of travelling performers.

13:45.080 --> 13:46.760
My, why is a girl like that here?

13:46.820 --> 13:48.760
Does she think it's right to come here?

13:48.380 --> 13:49.420
Who does she think she is?

14:01.450 --> 14:03.840
<i>I can't do my dance to this music.</i>

14:05.300 --> 14:07.360
Do you dislike the waltz?

14:07.530 --> 14:09.870
Nobody wants to
dance with a girl like that.

14:10.620 --> 14:12.540
Well, that's true, isn't it?

14:14.450 --> 14:15.780
<i>That's cruel...</i>

14:16.220 --> 14:17.790
Oh my! Pardon me.

14:20.390 --> 14:21.390
Oh, pardon.

14:41.460 --> 14:43.130
My little Rosebud.

14:45.500 --> 14:47.590
Look, it's me. We met this morning.

14:48.090 --> 14:48.920
Ah!

14:48.960 --> 14:50.670
Why are you in a place like this?

14:51.840 --> 14:52.860
I...

14:52.940 --> 14:55.640
Madame Monterlant told
me to perform my dance.

14:56.380 --> 14:57.920
That Madame Monterlant.

14:58.100 --> 14:59.500
She doesn't know when to stop.

15:01.950 --> 15:02.950
Alright.

15:03.700 --> 15:04.920
Come, in here.

15:05.210 --> 15:06.210
Eh?

15:06.390 --> 15:07.390
Umm...

15:07.430 --> 15:08.470
Don't worry.

15:08.550 --> 15:09.920
Leave it to us.

15:09.980 --> 15:11.320
B-But...

15:12.910 --> 15:13.910
It's Thierry.

15:14.690 --> 15:16.880
This dress is a sample.

15:17.540 --> 15:20.260
Monopolising Mr. Leo is not allowed.

15:20.400 --> 15:21.400
That's right!

15:21.430 --> 15:22.500
Huh?

15:23.710 --> 15:26.440
W-Wait a minute! You've got it wrong.

15:28.290 --> 15:30.770
Gentlemen, please wait outside.

15:33.960 --> 15:35.360
Well now.

15:36.360 --> 15:37.600
Umm...

15:38.030 --> 15:39.530
Are you ready?

15:39.610 --> 15:40.140
Eh?

15:40.490 --> 15:41.540
Here we go!

15:43.340 --> 15:44.340
Huh?

15:53.190 --> 15:54.340
Thanks for waiting.

15:54.990 --> 15:56.880
What do you think of this?

15:57.950 --> 15:58.650
Oh.

15:58.690 --> 15:59.690
This is...

15:59.800 --> 16:01.480
Très bien!

16:05.270 --> 16:06.980
America is the future.

16:07.510 --> 16:10.300
I've heard about some good
investments. Are you interested?

16:11.080 --> 16:14.160
Ladies and gentlemen, may
I have your attention please!

16:14.620 --> 16:17.180
Drawn here by the
gathering of the Black Roses,

16:17.540 --> 16:20.480
is a Rosebud on the verge of blooming!

16:34.400 --> 16:36.280
What sublime beauty!

16:36.350 --> 16:38.770
I wonder which noble
house that lady hails from?

16:54.630 --> 16:57.140
The miraculous dancer
of the Dandelion Troupe:

16:57.680 --> 16:58.890
Lady Nadja!

17:03.550 --> 17:04.880
The one from earlier?

17:06.670 --> 17:09.670
How dare that girl
draw attention to herself?

17:09.710 --> 17:10.800
Madame, this is–

17:10.910 --> 17:11.910
For me?

17:20.930 --> 17:26.080
"Tonight, I've come to take the
beautiful Madame Monterlant's necklace."

17:26.190 --> 17:27.190
"-Black Rose."

17:28.160 --> 17:29.160
Eh?

17:30.370 --> 17:31.140
How...

17:31.290 --> 17:32.760
How splendid!

17:33.180 --> 17:35.440
Who is the one with the sense of style?

17:35.460 --> 17:39.280
Sending such a thing
to liven up tonight's party.

17:40.240 --> 17:41.320
What a relief.

17:41.980 --> 17:43.220
It's just a prank.

17:43.520 --> 17:45.640
It's you, isn't it? Antonio Fabian.

17:45.920 --> 17:46.980
Heaven forbid.

17:47.080 --> 17:49.980
I would never spend money on such a joke.

17:50.820 --> 17:52.240
I was nervous for a moment.

17:52.280 --> 17:55.420
Wasn't that quite the
surprise, my little Rosebud?

17:55.500 --> 17:57.000
But, my name is Nadja.

17:57.250 --> 17:59.180
You really are a spunky one, huh?

18:02.040 --> 18:03.040
A blackout!

18:03.910 --> 18:05.040
What's going on?

18:05.060 --> 18:06.980
Eh? What was that?

18:11.920 --> 18:13.550
The necklace...

18:13.860 --> 18:15.300
The necklace is...

18:15.420 --> 18:16.560
Gone!

18:16.740 --> 18:18.220
Eh?

18:18.650 --> 18:20.800
Black Rose. It's Black Rose!

18:20.960 --> 18:23.460
The note was genuine!

18:23.820 --> 18:24.920
Aunt?

18:25.280 --> 18:27.200
The real Black Rose?

18:28.220 --> 18:30.170
I can't believe you went so far!

18:30.490 --> 18:32.220
A magnificent piece of playacting,

18:32.420 --> 18:33.520
Madame Monterlant.

18:37.370 --> 18:39.090
It's a play? That's great!

18:39.800 --> 18:41.760
I was quite startled.

18:41.880 --> 18:43.800
N-No, it's not.

18:45.440 --> 18:48.660
For sponsoring such a splendid evening,

18:48.780 --> 18:51.300
we give thanks to Madame Monterlant!

19:11.100 --> 19:12.670
May I have this dance?

19:22.540 --> 19:23.760
Umm...

19:25.980 --> 19:28.140
<i>What does he want? He's so forceful.</i>

19:28.580 --> 19:29.770
<i>But very good.</i>

19:29.910 --> 19:32.370
<i>My body feels as light as a feather.</i>

19:32.800 --> 19:35.170
<i>This feeling, where have I?</i>

19:35.450 --> 19:38.010
Why are you in a place like this?

19:38.410 --> 19:39.410
Eh?

19:39.560 --> 19:43.940
Wearing such a beautiful dress, and coming
to this absurd party. Do you find it fun?

19:44.350 --> 19:45.480
It's not...

19:46.100 --> 19:47.270
I didn't have a choice.

19:47.650 --> 19:49.800
You must not come to places like these.

19:50.260 --> 19:52.660
To a place so contaminated
with wealth and greed.

19:58.320 --> 19:59.400
Ah?!

19:59.980 --> 20:01.950
B-Black Rose? The real one?

20:04.520 --> 20:07.100
You stole it, didn't you?

20:07.160 --> 20:08.530
That necklace.

20:08.830 --> 20:10.400
What if I did?

20:10.520 --> 20:14.060
Why don't you shout
"Black Rose is right here!"?

20:14.380 --> 20:15.500
Why?

20:15.640 --> 20:17.440
Why do you steal?

20:18.160 --> 20:19.360
Look at that woman.

20:19.500 --> 20:20.820
You're Black Rose, aren't you?

20:21.130 --> 20:23.010
Yes. I am Black Rose.

20:23.700 --> 20:24.560
Is it you?

20:24.680 --> 20:26.320
Of course, I too, am Black Rose.

20:26.610 --> 20:28.900
The woman has too much money,

20:28.980 --> 20:31.220
and she wastes her time
playing around every day.

20:31.650 --> 20:35.790
But, for those poor people living
in desperation at the same time,

20:35.830 --> 20:38.480
she doesn't even think to use 1 franc.

20:38.870 --> 20:41.320
The other noblemen and
the wealthy are quite similar.

20:43.060 --> 20:46.220
People really are all equal,
no matter who they may be.

20:46.710 --> 20:49.700
So, in order for everyone
to live equally, I steal.

20:52.190 --> 20:55.220
But, even if you say it's for the poor,

20:55.260 --> 20:57.650
there are other ways than stealing!

20:58.270 --> 21:01.990
I don't like to do the same
thing as everyone else.

21:06.380 --> 21:08.340
Good bye, little girl.

21:17.920 --> 21:19.340
The police!

21:19.360 --> 21:21.990
Someone call the police, please!

21:22.520 --> 21:25.660
This was truly a perfect staging, my Aunt!

21:30.060 --> 21:31.840
"Black Rose appears!"

21:33.270 --> 21:36.760
"Madame Monterlant's necklace stolen!"

21:37.120 --> 21:38.440
As I thought, he's in Paris.

21:39.730 --> 21:41.730
I was right to come home.

21:43.350 --> 21:44.850
Several days later.

21:44.890 --> 21:47.840
A rumor about Black
Rose reachs Nadja's ears.

21:48.010 --> 21:53.810
He had distributed large amounts
of money to the town's poor.

21:54.810 --> 21:57.800
People really are all equal,
no matter who they may be.

21:58.570 --> 22:00.960
<i>Black Rose may not be a bad person.</i>

22:01.580 --> 22:02.580
<i>No.</i>

22:02.930 --> 22:04.340
<i>But, that person is...</i>

22:14.490 --> 22:16.115
Paris is sunnier than London

22:16.116 --> 22:17.740
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:17.860 --> 22:20.950
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:21.370 --> 22:24.455
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:24.456 --> 22:27.540
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:28.500 --> 22:29.740
- Indeed
- Kitto

22:32.500 --> 22:34.920
- It's not use worrying about it
- Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:35.500 --> 22:37.065
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:37.066 --> 22:38.630
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:38.890 --> 22:41.245
Tomorrow's going to
be whatever it was meant

22:41.246 --> 22:43.600
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:43.680 --> 22:45.060
- To be, to be
- Naru naru

22:45.390 --> 22:47.895
The tree fog won

22:47.896 --> 22:50.400
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:50.860 --> 22:52.820
The world frog-jumping contest

22:52.821 --> 22:54.780
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:57.990 --> 23:01.075
Under the kitten's paw

23:01.076 --> 23:04.160
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:04.580 --> 23:07.665
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:07.666 --> 23:10.750
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:13.590 --> 23:15.255
Paris is sunnier than London

23:15.256 --> 23:16.920
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.010 --> 23:20.010
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:20.510 --> 23:23.700
It's not the time to hang around

23:23.701 --> 23:26.890
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:27.770 --> 23:30.020
Indeed, indeed

23:30.021 --> 23:32.270
Kitto kitto

23:40.000 --> 23:41.540
- Tomorrow's Nadja
- Tomorrow's Nadja

23:41.570 --> 23:43.709
Sylvie, did you know?

23:43.710 --> 23:46.580
All people have invisible wings.

23:46.910 --> 23:48.410
Raphael said so.

23:49.010 --> 23:50.790
You like him, don't you?

23:51.230 --> 23:52.800
Why don't you tell him?

23:53.750 --> 23:55.300
Eh? Me?

23:56.740 --> 23:59.749
But, I only danced with Francis once.

23:59.750 --> 24:02.050
He might just forget about me.

24:02.810 --> 24:03.600
Tomorrow's Nadja:

24:03.601 --> 24:06.160
Broken Wing and Tears of Love.

24:06.350 --> 24:08.330
Now, the Door of Destiny opens.
